reims-manager (1.0.2-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a Reims Manager GTK theme so the native interface has a consistent
    appearance across desktop themes.
  * Limit physical USB passthrough to four devices and exclude virtual inputs.
  * Match Apple USB devices by physical port when possible and suppress the
    duplicate row produced when an iPhone re-enumerates on that port.
  * Show slot use in both interfaces and check capacity before host release.
  * Select update assets by package format and document the groundwork and
    limitations for distro update managers and Apple Watch support.

 -- phuf2012 <245987108+phuf2012@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0600

reims-manager (1.0.2-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep prerelease builds out of the update channel for stable installs.
  * Add a Reims vGPU accelerated graphics backend choice and a VMware SVGA
    compatibility fallback to both settings interfaces.
  * Add device-specific unlock and Trust guidance for iPhone and iPad passthrough.
  * Clarify that GitHub update links use HTTPS and that Mint Update Manager
    needs a signed APT repository, which this release does not configure.
  * Document Apple Watch passthrough as a future research item, not a working
    feature, because watch pairing is managed through a paired iPhone.

 -- phuf2012 <245987108+phuf2012@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0600

reims-manager (1.0.2-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Detect the VM's actual USB controller and use its bus for hotplug.
  * Find mounted partitions through their parent USB disk before unmounting.
  * Request a tree-form disk list so Linux reports each partition under its disk.
  * Show the available guest passthrough controller in USB diagnostics.

